1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,000
VNBank-LOD is a five-star Linked Open Data dataset of Vietnamese banks, developed by Group 24.

2
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:14,000
The project follows all five steps, from ontology design and data collection to interlinking and querying.

3
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:21,000
The dataset covers thirty banks and combines public sources with manual verification against official bank websites.

4
00:00:21,000 --> 00:00:28,000
Every external link records its verification method, evidence and confidence level.

5
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:35,000
The original ontology graph visualises the schema, defined classes, datatypes and schema.org alignment.

6
00:00:35,000 --> 00:00:42,000
The original instance graph shows ACB and Vietcombank connected to types, locations, services and external resources.

7
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:49,000
The overview graph connects all thirty banks with inferred categories and headquarters locations.

8
00:00:49,000 --> 00:00:56,000
This Protégé class hierarchy confirms that the ontology and schema.org alignment were edited and inspected directly.

9
00:00:56,000 --> 00:01:03,000
With the HermiT reasoner active, the defined DigitalBank class is classified from its equivalent class expression.

10
00:01:03,000 --> 00:01:10,000
The inverseOf axiom explicitly connects isHeadquartersOf with hasHeadquarters.

11
00:01:10,000 --> 00:01:17,000
Show Inferences reveals service-to-bank assertions inferred from the inverse property model.

12
00:01:17,000 --> 00:01:25,000
The script loads the Turtle file, runs OWL RL reasoning, every quality check and two sample queries.

13
00:01:25,000 --> 00:01:30,000
Q1 lists all thirty banks with bilingual names.

14
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:35,000
Q2 retrieves state-owned commercial banks through inferred class membership.

15
00:01:35,000 --> 00:01:40,000
Q3 returns the twenty banks headquartered in Hanoi without duplicate external IRIs.

16
00:01:40,000 --> 00:01:45,000
Q4 identifies banks classified as digital banks.

17
00:01:45,000 --> 00:01:50,000
Q5 uses a datatype filter to find banks established before 1991.

18
00:01:50,000 --> 00:01:55,000
Q6 lists verified owl:sameAs links to Wikidata and DBpedia.

19
00:01:55,000 --> 00:02:00,000
Q7 demonstrates inverse reasoning from services back to their providers.

20
00:02:00,000 --> 00:02:05,000
Q8 demonstrates inverse headquarters reasoning and returns twenty Hanoi banks.

21
00:02:05,000 --> 00:02:10,000
Q9 uses COUNT, GROUP BY and ORDER BY to aggregate banks by type.

22
00:02:10,000 --> 00:02:15,000
Q10 uses ASK and confirms that external Linked Data connections exist.

23
00:02:15,000 --> 00:02:20,000
Q11 uses CONSTRUCT to create a reusable bank-service subgraph.

24
00:02:20,000 --> 00:02:25,000
Q12 uses FILTER NOT EXISTS to find banks lacking external links.

25
00:02:25,000 --> 00:02:30,000
Q13 uses UNION to combine state-owned and foreign-owned bank categories.

26
00:02:30,000 --> 00:02:35,000
Q14 uses DESCRIBE to export the complete local description of ACB.

27
00:02:35,000 --> 00:02:40,000
Q15 uses SERVICE to retrieve English labels and inception dates from Wikidata.

28
00:02:40,000 --> 00:02:45,000
Q16 is typed freely into the SPARQL terminal and counts banks by headquarters city.

29
00:02:45,000 --> 00:02:55,000
The final dataset contains thirty banks, thirty-eight external links, sixteen demonstrated queries and zero quality violations.

30
00:02:55,000 --> 00:03:05,000
VNBank-LOD demonstrates semantic modelling, automated inference and operational five-star data integration.
